<h2>Catechist's Guide</h2>
<p class="big-question">For class preparation and delivery. For the catechist's use only.</p>

<h3>Class Summary</h3>

<p><strong>Estimated duration:</strong> 60 minutes</p>
<p><strong>Central theme:</strong> The liturgy as an encounter with Christ, in whom the Paschal Mystery works through signs and sacraments.</p>
<p><strong>Objectives:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Understand that the liturgy is the work of Christ, not a human invention.</li>
<li>Discover the Paschal Mystery as the heart of every liturgical celebration.</li>
<li>Distinguish between the common and ministerial priesthood.</li>
<li>Value liturgical signs and the Liturgical Year.</li>
<li>Participate actively in Mass, not as a spectator but as a protagonist.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Key verse:</strong> <em>&laquo;They devoted themselves to the apostles' teaching and to fellowship, to the breaking of bread and to prayer&raquo;</em> (Acts 2:42)</p>
<p><strong>CCC references:</strong> 1066-1134, 1085, 1090, 1141-1178</p>

</section>

